   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 6. Clips and audio references (version 3)\nA version-3 view set can hold **up to 3 clips**, each with an optional **soundtrack**, and **up to 3 standalone audio references** (a voice, music, ambience), next to any views. Audio is stored as the H3 audio VAE's latent: the text encoder never hears audio (it only gets an `<Audio j>: ` label), so the stored latent is exactly what the native reference node hands the DiT. Replay is bit-identical to *MiniMax H3 Reference to Video* fed the same files.\n\n**Build (top row, muted)**\n1. *Load Video* + *Get Video Components* give a clip's frames and soundtrack: connect them to `orbit` (clip 1) and `orbit_audio`. `clip_2` / `clip_3` and their `_audio` inputs take two more; folders of frames work too (`orbit_folder`, `clip_2_folder`, ...).\n2. *Load Audio* reads audio files **and the audio track of a video**: connect up to three to `audio_1..3`. A voice reference works best as a standalone audio; a soundtrack is not cut to `orbit_length` (the native node doesn't either), so trim it with *Trim Audio Duration* if it is long. Any audio needs the `audio_vae`.\n3. Set `name`, unmute (Ctrl+M), queue once, mute again, refresh the browser so the file appears in `viewset`.\n\n**Generate**\n- `audios`: which standalone audio references to add (`1`, `1,2` or `all`); `orbit` and `more_clips` add clips. The **Label guide** lists the `<Audio j>` and `<Video k>` labels in the order the native node numbers them: a clip's soundtrack takes an `<Audio j>` before any standalone audio.\n- Bind the reference in the prompt, as here: `<Audio 1> is the voice of <Subject 1>.` in `subject_definitions`, and a `retention_analysis` line for it. Put the spoken words in the shot as `(S1) <d>[English] ...</d>`.\n\n**Measured** (H3-rendered voices, a back-turned subject, 3 seeds; speaker similarity, where same-source halves score 0.61):\n\n| reference | similarity to it |\n|---|---|\n| none | 0.07 to voice A, 0.29 to voice B |\n| voice A as `<Audio 1>` | **0.58** to A |\n| voice A's clip with its soundtrack | 0.45 to A, at 20x the tokens |\n| voice B as `<Audio 1>` | **0.67** to B |\n| a cello piece as `<Audio 1>` | copied verbatim on 1 of 3 seeds, which dropped the dialogue |\n\n**So the voice follows a standalone audio reference**, and the prompt's line is still the one spoken. Real speakers, and a voice against a contrary look (a deep voice for a child), are untested. A voice identifies a person as much as a face: use voices with consent.\n\n**Settings in these workflows** follow ComfyUI's MiniMax H3 reference-to-video template: the ref2va model with its 4-step Lightning LoRA, 4 steps, `res_multistep` + `simple`, 608x352. For the base model, bypass the *Lightning LoRA* node and use 20 steps. The measurements quoted here ran on a community H3 turbo finetune (shift 6/3, 8 steps) on a 12 GB GPU. Raise the size and length for final renders; the reference tokens ride through every step, so more photos and larger captures cost time."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
